From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:06:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc CONFIG screen from the original Game.exe
 (OptionsMenuType.SGHD)

The STEINS;GATE (Steam) CONFIG screen as the original draws and handles it, instead of the 0023 fallback that left
CONFIG at once. All layout, art, value ranges, steps and behaviour come from the original Game.exe: the page draw
routines (basic / text 0x438ef0, sound 0x438240, character voices 0x438a60, tabs 0x43b490; drawSprite 0x432230,
stretched draw 0x432710), the input routine (0x439b00..) and the defaults (0x438030..). Texts are part of the
(localised) CONFIG.DDS sheet, so translated data shows its own language.

- New generic class UI::SGHD::OptionsMenu + Profile::SGHD::OptionsMenu (OptionsMenuType.SGHD): pages, rows
  (toggle, slider, choice, radio, character voice) and tabs are all profile data; no layout in the code.
- Behaviour as the original: shown while the script fades submenu 5 in (SW_SYSSUBMENUNO / SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA, from
  the title or the system menu); the screen owns the input while fully shown; Back raises SF_SUBMENUEXIT and writes
  the system data (the original keeps these values in it); every page has its own cursor, starting with none; up /
  down wrap; Q / E (L1 / R1) and the tabs change page with the original 32 frame sideways slide; sliders show a half
  transparent knob at the value the screen opened with; text speed 256..4096 step 30, auto wait 256..2048 step 14,
  volumes 0..128 step 1; mouse / touch: hover or tap moves the cursor, tap toggles, drag sets a slider; the
  original's hit areas (labels column for on / off rows).
- Settings: phone trigger skip release, TIPS notification, auto quick save (scene), skip mode, text and auto speed,
  voice / BGM / SE / movie volume, voice sync, skip voice, the 12 per-character voice volumes and on / off marks.
  Window mode and resolution show the fixed state (full screen, 1920x1080) as they have no meaning here.
- CC title menu: does not take input while another screen opened from the title has the menu focus (it is updated
  before the options screen and swallowed its clicks).
- 0023's CONFIG fallback (raise SF_SUBMENUEXIT at once) now only applies when the profile has no options menu.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15, original English data): CONFIG from the title and from the system menu shows the
original pages (layout matches screenshots of the original game), page slide with E / Q, taps toggle, slider drag,
Backspace returns to the title / system menu, the screen can be reopened, a changed setting survives a restart;
mo6tw-pc-zhs title, new game and system menu unchanged.

